<title>FRANCE: French Jan M3 money supply fell 0.5 percent.</title>
<headline>French Jan M3 money supply fell 0.5 percent.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of France gave the following money supply figures:</p>
<p> Money measure  Billions   Monthly change    12-month change</p>
<p>(end-Jan)	(unadj)	(adjusted)	   Jan	 Dec</p>
<p>    M1	    1,684.2	 -2.2		 0.8	 0.4</p>
<p>    M2	    3,263.2	 -0.3		 3.3	 3.3</p>
<p>    M3	    5,254.5	 -0.5		-2.9	-2.4</p>
<p>    M4	    5,346.1	 -0.5		-2.7	-2.2</p>
<p>Investment</p>
<p>    P1	    1,957.9	  1.8		17.2	16.8</p>
<p> Credit measure		billions monthly change  yr/yr change</p>
<p>  (end-Dec)		    (unadj)   Dec   Nov	     Dec</p>
<p> Total domestic debt	10,832.1  -0.1   0.8	     2.6</p>
<p> Total credits to economy  6,347.3  -1.2   0.6	    -2.5</p>
<p>The Bank revised the monthly fall in M3 money supply in December to -1.0 percent from -0.9.</p>
<p>The central bank has set a ceiling on M3 growth of five percent a year on average over the next few years.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 53 81</p>
</text>
